One of my friend recently appeared for Infosys interview and
Here’s a summary of the L1 round interview questions along with short answers that might help others preparing. 

L1 Interview Questions & Answers

1. Tell me about yourself
Ans) Shared my experience in Automation Testing, skills (Java, Selenium, TestNG, Maven), framework design, and exposure to Agile methodology.

2. Describe your project and your role
Ans)Explain automation framework development, test case design, execution, reporting, CI/CD integration, and defect management.

3. Are you designing the framework? Explain its folder structure
Ans) Yes. Standard folders: src/main/java (base, utilities, page classes), src/test/java (test scripts), resources (config, test data), reports.

4. What type of framework are you using?
Ans)Hybrid framework (POM + Data Driven + TestNG).

5. What is the Maven command you use?
Ans) mvn clean test (to clean old builds and run test cases).

6. Write a program to reverse a string
Ans)Using StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(str); sb.reverse();.

7. Automation Scenario (Amazon – search mobiles, scroll, find 7th item XPath)
Ans) Use Actions or JavascriptExecutor for scrolling, and generic XPath 

8. Validate multiple mobile numbers on a site
Ans) Use regex ([0-9]{10}) to check validity, loop through list, maintain counters for valid/invalid.

9. Selenium program to read data from Excel
Ans) Use Apache POI library to read rows/cells and pass data into tests.

10. Difference between method overloading & overriding
Ans)
Overloading → Same method name, different parameters (compile-time polymorphism).
Overriding → Same method signature, child class modifies parent method (runtime polymorphism).

11. Primary key vs Foreign key
Ans) Primary key → uniquely identifies rows in a table.
Foreign key → establishes relationship between two tables referencing primary key.

12. HTTP Status codes
Ans)200 → Success, 201 → Created, 400 → Bad Request, 401 → Unauthorized, 404 → Not Found, 500 → Server Error.

13. HTTP method calls
Ans) GET (fetch), POST (create), PUT (update), DELETE (remove).

14. What is inheritance? Where do you apply it in framework?
Ans) Inheritance → acquiring properties from parent class. Used in framework for BaseClass (WebDriver setup, common methods) extended by TestClasses.

15. Explain testng.xml file
Ans) XML file to configure suites, groups, parameterization, parallel execution, and test order
